## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Question 1: `../skills/...` references in `django/agents/*.agent.md`**
> 
> The Django agent files reference skills using `../skills/django-models/SKILL.md`. This is an **intra-package relative path** (from `django/agents/` up to `django/skills/`), NOT a cross-package escape. When you copy `django/` into `backend-project-a/`, the path `../skills/` resolves to `backend-project-a/skills/` — which is correct.
> 
> Should I leave these as-is (they work correctly after copy), or normalize to root-relative paths like `skills/django-models/SKILL.md`?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Question 2: `foundation/` directories**
> 
> The user requirement says "Do not put framework code in the agent template" and to keep starter code under `templates/`. Should I:
> - **(A)** Rename `foundation/` to `templates/foundation/` across all packages, or
> - **(B)** Keep `foundation/` where it is but add clear documentation that it is optional template/starter code (not agent infrastructure)?
> 
> Option B is lower-risk and preserves the existing `update-agent.sh` scripts that reference `foundation/`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Question 3: Flutter parent `AGENTS.md`**
> 
> `flutter/AGENTS.md` is a thin router pointing to `desktop/AGENTS.md` and `mobile/AGENTS.md`. When copying `flutter/mobile/` standalone, this parent file is not included. The user requirement says `flutter/mobile/` must be independently copyable. The mobile `AGENTS.md` is already self-sufficient. Should I:
> - **(A)** Leave `flutter/AGENTS.md` as-is (it's only useful in the full repository), or
> - **(B)** Remove it entirely?

